  "body": "## What changed\n\nSlice 5 (last) of #1440: the setup's own page (`SetupPage::Settings`, the \"Setup1\" node's properties page) follows the WCS page's layout. This is NOT the \"Setups\" list page (`pages.rs::setups_page`), a different page that stays as it is.\n\n- Titled `layout::group` sections: Active setup, Stock source, Part orientation (with a one-line helper), Work offset, Workholding (only for a turning setup or one that states a limit), This setup (Delete / Open fixtures as two equal-width `even_row` buttons), then the stock entity / datum line as a small readout at the foot.\n- With no setups the page is the one \"First setup\" group (message, pointer line, \"Create first setup\" button).\n- New `setup_settings_page.rs` (the page body left `setup_pages.rs`). The pickers keep their controls and captions; the groups frame them. `setup_stock_pick` lost its bare \"Stock\" caption (the group title says it); `setup_workholding_row::shown` is the row's own test; `wcs_page::cell_w` is `pub(super)`.\n- Page-wide indent 12 and item gap 4: the pick rows are as wide as the narrow pane (#330) and the default indent pushed \"Point 1 to plane level\" and the workholding Apply past its edge (the existing structural tests caught both).\n- Layout only: no command, parameter or project-file change; every edit goes through its existing undoable command. No snapshot PNG touched.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1440-setup-page-tidy.md`.\n\n## Series\n\nThe five pages of #1440: Stock #1460, Tool list #1465, Fixtures #1471, Machine #1472, Setup (this PR). `Refs #1440` only; the issue closes when all five merge.\n\n## Overlap (stacking decision)\n\n#773 (orientation dropdowns) changes five lines inside the old `settings()` (replaces the alignment, plane, points and axis calls with one `setup_orient_pick::section`). Not stacked: it is a contributor's draft on another fork (cannot push to it) and this PR moves those lines into the new file, so one small hunk resolves at whichever merges second (the call list goes into the \"Part orientation\" group). Expected textual overlaps: `setup_pages.rs` (#773, #1465, #1472; this PR deletes `settings()` and removes the `UiTarget` import), `wcs_page.rs` (`cell_w` `pub(super)`, the same one-line change as #1472, identical so it merges clean), `mod.rs` / `tests.rs` (module lists, adjacent additions), `setup_stock_pick.rs` and `setup_workholding_row.rs` (small). #1209 and #1124 touch `pages.rs` and the WCS flow, not this page.\n\n## Pins (crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_settings_page.rs)\n\n- the_setup_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page: every group title in order; every label/button of every picker inside its own group in order; two equal action buttons on one row; foot readout.\n- the_first_setups_page_has_no_previous_setup_rows (fresh/first setup: stock note, no relative / \"leaves behind\" rows).\n- an_inactive_setups_page_draws_its_groups_and_the_radio_activates_it (inactive setup; radio click and undo).\n- the_page_with_no_setups_offers_only_the_first_setup (empty document; button and undo).\n- a_lathe_setup_draws_the_workholding_group (conditional group; Apply rpm then Clear rpm / Stated).\n- the_armed_pick_rows_stay_inside_their_groups (plane, points and WCS armed rows: every conditionally drawn control).\n- the_setup_actions_still_queue_their_commands, open_fixtures_activates_the_setup_and_opens_its_fixtures_page.\n\nMutation check (each mutation applied alone to `setup_settings_page.rs`, the 8 tests run): all 19 went red: dropped active radio, stock group, helper line, alignment / relative / plane / points / axes / work offset / WCS-features calls, workholding group (absent and always drawn), Delete command, Open fixtures focus, foot readout, Create first setup command, no-setups message, pointer line, a reordered Work offset group. Stays green / unpinned: the Primary, Apply axes and Clear axes rows (drawn only after an axis pick in the viewport, which needs a real face pick) and the group-title text of a collapsed group.\n\n## Not exercised / known\n\n- Pane still scrolls sideways on the long axes caption (unchanged, pre-existing).\n- Space-padded pick captions (\"    Part alignment\") untouched: nine files that #773 / #746 also edit, and their tests match the padded strings.\n\n## Gates\n\nfork synced at v0.19-line main (branched from upstream/main 7c21c9c2). `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` ok (63 s); camcraft-ui lib single-threaded from `crates/ui`: 682 passed; clippy `-p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Screenshots: before/after attached below\n\n(before.png / after.png: Setup2 of a seeded document; before-empty.png / after-empty.png: a fresh document's Setup1. Local copies in ~/Desktop/camcraft/builds/pr-1440-setup/.)\n\nChangelog: Setup page follows the WCS page's layout: titled groups, equal action buttons, a readout at the foot, a \"First setup\" group with no setups (#1440, PR #1476)\n\nRefs #1440\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
